# How to cite SymQ. The version below follows pyproject.toml (a test compares them).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SymQ in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "SymQ: exact Boolean ANF and reversible-circuit verification"
abstract: >-
  SymQ computes exact algebraic normal forms of X/CX/CCX/MCX reversible circuits and decides
  their equivalence, with pure-Python and optional native C/ZDD backends and a separate SAT
  engine. Each checker proves one named theorem.
authors:
  - family-names: Melka
    given-names: Joshua
version: 0.2.0.dev0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yoch/symq"
url: "https://github.com/yoch/symq"
keywords:
  - boolean algebra
  - algebraic normal form
  - reversible circuits
  - formal verification
  - zero-suppressed decision diagrams
